    thinking: "**Initiating Pantry Guard Design**\n\nI\'m starting to visualize the \"Pantry Guard\" application. The core focus right now is on the Dashboard or Inventory list. I\'m thinking about the layout and how the filter tabs will work to provide a streamlined experience. I need to make sure it\'s intuitive and easy to use.\n\n\n**Refining Inventory View**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the dashboard\'s features. Specifically, I\'m fleshing out the filter and sort functionality\342\200\224expiry date, name, and quantity sorting are key. The item cards will show expiry status visually. I\'m also planning a FAB for product addition, plus export and share buttons. The plan includes \"Actual,\" \"Pr\303\263ximo a Caducar,\" \"Caducados,\" and \"Todos\" filters. A search bar is essential.\n\n\n\n**Developing Item Detail Screens**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the item detail screen design. I\'ve got the data fields nailed down: item name, categories, quantity, units, expiration date (with picker), and storage location. Barcode input and scanner are crucial. There are save/delete buttons with toast feedback. I\'m focusing on user flows for adding, editing, and deleting items, which will be essential to provide a good user experience.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 953733927
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
