  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining React Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the React components needed for the application. Currently, I\'m outlining the specific components, starting with `TopAppBar.tsx`. I\'m breaking down its structure, including the logo, title, share button with fallback, notifications trigger, and the data status icon.\n\n\n**Designing Navigation Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing the navigation elements. I\'ve begun outlining the `BottomNavBar.tsx` with its three tabs: Dashboard, Compras, and Perfil. I\'m focusing on active state styles, a pill indicator, and smooth transitions, considering both mobile-fixed bottom and desktop compatibility. Also, `DashboardView.tsx` is being elaborated, including search bar, filter tabs, header with products count, filter options and bento grid cards displaying product information and status.\n\n\n**Adding Product Input**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user input experience for products. I\'ve specified a Floating Action Button for adding new products, an export PDF button, and a quick scan button. I\'m deep into the `BarcodeScannerModal.tsx`, implementing a functional camera scanner with fallback options and a dynamic UI including a viewfinder, flashlight toggle, and manual input. I\'m also looking at the success logic, haptic feedback, and auto-population of the product modal. Finally, I\'m working on `ProductModal.tsx` itself.\n\n\n**Elaborating Product & Shopping View**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of product entry and the shopping list view. I\'m focusing on the `ProductModal.tsx`, including detailed input fields for product categories, quantity, unit, location, expiry date, and barcode scanning with camera integration. I\'m also implementing \"Guardar\" and \"Eliminar\" buttons with validation and toast animations. On `ShoppingListView.tsx`, I\'m designing the header, filter chips, and shopping item cards with status indicators, quantity badges, and add/check toggles. A search input for adding more products and a button to generate the list are also in progress.\n\n\n**Finalizing Profile & Preferences**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"\302\241Lista Generada!\" success modal, complete with PDF download and share features. I\'m also now designing the `ProfileView.tsx`, focusing on the user avatar, name, and email details. I\'m building bento navigation cards for account settings, shared households, and app preferences, alongside a \"Cerrar sesi\303\263n\" button. Further, I\'m working on the `PreferencesView.tsx`, with language and appearance options as radio buttons, dark mode toggle, and metric vs imperial unit selection cards. Finally, the \"Guardar Cambios\" button has also been included. Lastly, I am building the `SharedHouseholdView.tsx`, focusing on managing household members.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 462507582
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
