  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Error State**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the root cause of the `Uncaught Cannot clear while scan is ongoing, close it first.` error. It seems `Html5Qrcode` relies on an internal state machine that transitions through `UNKNOWN`, `NOT_STARTED`, `SCANNING`, and `PAUSED`. The problem occurs when `clear()` is called while the state is actively `SCANNING`.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Race Condition**\n\nI\'ve discovered a race condition within the cleanup function. Because `stop()` is asynchronous, `clear()` is often called before `stop()` completes, causing the \"Cannot clear while scan is ongoing\" error. Furthermore, if `start()` is still in progress when the modal closes, calling `clear()` or `stop()` throws an error even though `isScanning` is false. This also occurs in the `handleScanDone` function and is exacerbated by `scanner.getState()` returning `SCANNING`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 320972570
    }
