    thinking: "**Analyzing Scanner Lifecycle**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the `BarcodeScannerModal`. I\'m analyzing the lifecycle of the `Html5Qrcode` scanner instance when the modal is closed. It appears the scanner might still be running during the modal\'s cleanup phase, and this may be creating problems. I\'m focusing on the `useEffect` hook and the asynchronous calls, which may be where I can resolve the issue.\n\n\n**Investigating Scanner State Transitions**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into potential race conditions with the scanner\'s state transitions. Specifically, I\'m concerned about scenarios where `start()` resolves after the component is unmounted, potentially leading to issues. The `isScanning` state and the sequence of `start()`, `stop()`, and `clear()` calls require precise control. I need to make sure `clear()` isn\'t invoked during scanning or container removal. I am thinking of using the `html5-qrcode` best practices.\n\n\n**Refining Scanner Shutdown Logic**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously reviewing the scanner\'s shutdown sequence. I\'ve placed asynchronous `stop()` and `clear()` calls within `useEffect`\'s cleanup function, and also `handleScanDone` so that they do not block unmounts. I\'m focusing on handling potential errors from `stop()` and `clear()` gracefully using try-catch blocks. I\'m also ensuring the `scannerContainerId` is safely present before attempting to start the scanner, and nullifying the scanner reference after cleanup. I am focused on the asynchronous calls and unmounting.\n\n\n"
