  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing HTML5Qrcode**\n\nI\'m currently observing the behavior of `Html5Qrcode` within `BarcodeScannerModal.tsx`. It seems that when rendered into `#pantry-guard-barcode-reader`, `Html5Qrcode` introduces a video element and frequently adds its container alongside other elements. Screenshot 1 illustrates this process.\n\n\n**Examining the UI Issues**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause: the `Html5Qrcode` library, when rendered, generates a `<video>` element that isn\'t styled by default. This video stretches to the full resolution of the camera. The modal, lacking `overflow: hidden`, allows the video to expand, causing scrollbars and a distorted UI. Furthermore, the `shadow-` class, particularly the large shadow, exacerbates the problem, as the browser extends the scrollable overflow box.\n\n\n**Refining Layout Solutions**\n\nI\'m now considering fixes for the reticle and camera layout. The problematic `9999px` box-shadow is being swapped out. I\'m focusing on alternatives: SVG masks, dark overlays, or ensuring the modal has `overflow-hidden`. Also, a cleaner reticle design with a tinted background is being investigated. I\'m thinking of adding CSS to `index.css` for more explicit control over the video element\'s sizing and positioning, using `width: 100%`, `height: 100%`, `object-fit: cover` and absolute positioning.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 925377148
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
