  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Listing Gemini Models**\n\nI\'ve been compiling a list of the supported models within `@google/genai` specifically for text and multimodal applications. Currently, the options are `gemini-2.5-flash`, which is considered a standard model, alongside the more powerful `gemini-2.5-pro` for complex reasoning tasks. I am documenting the full range of supported models.\n\n\n**Expanding Model Coverage**\n\nI\'ve added `gemini-lite`, `gemini-2.0-flash`, `gemini-2.0-flash-lite`, and `gemini-3.7-flash` to the model list. Considering how to handle high demand, I\'m implementing retries with jitter and exponential backoff, cascading through available models. I also want to cache the results and prevent console spam. Additionally, I\'ll gracefully handle API errors with concise warnings, and default to local analysis when all models are unavailable, so the user interface never breaks.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 840552385
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
