  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Product Definition**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `types.ts` file to examine the `Product` definition. I\'m considering adding optional properties: `brand`, `imageUrl`, and `nutriScore` to the `Product` type. The goal is to see how these additions align with the existing structure and ensure compatibility.\n\n\n**Refining Barcode Lookup**\n\nI\'m expanding the scope of my investigation. Now I\'m looking at the enhancements for the `BarcodeLookupResult`, considering fields like `ingredients` and `source` to improve data enrichment. I\'m focusing on open food facts to add the real integration details, including the API call, timeout handling, and header configuration to improve request reliability. Further, I\'m working on the data extraction logic, specifically, how to parse `product_name` and handle brand information using fallbacks. I\'m building out a list of categories to support richer keyword mapping.\n\n\n**Categorizing and Parsing Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on categorizing food items, creating lists for fruits, vegetables, proteins, grains, beverages, and others, including both Spanish and English terms. I\'m also working on parsing quantities and units, extracting the quantity and unit from strings like \"1 L\" or \"500 g\". Furthermore, I\'m defining a strategy for determining the best image URL and calculating the nutri-score grade by converting it to uppercase. Finally, I\'m working on calculating smart expiration dates using benchmarks associated to different food categories.\n\n\n**Calculating Expiration Dates**\n\nI\'m now implementing expiration date calculations based on food categories. I\'m assigning shelf lives to fresh meat/fish (+5 days), canned goods and grains/pastas/cereals (+180 days), vegetables (+7 days), fruits (+6 days), beverages (+90 days), and other items (+30 days).\n\nI\'m also looking into a `pantry_learned_barcodes` strategy. This will save user-scanned and edited items. Finally, I\'m working to support a local catalog of popular Latam & Global Barcodes. I\'m building enhancements to the `BarcodeScannerModal.tsx` file for switching between scanner and image decode.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
