    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Barcode Decoding**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the barcode scanning process, specifically focusing on how ZXing handles image input in `imageBarcodeDecoder.ts`. I noticed the use of `TRY_HARDER: true` within `POSSIBLE_FORMATS`. This configuration triggers the instantiation of internal sub-readers for diverse barcode types such as QR codes, Aztec, PDF417, and Datamatrix to decode the image.\n\n\n**Developing Preprocessing Strategies**\n\nI\'ve been examining challenges in barcode scanning, like high-resolution images where barcodes are small, and glare issues. Also, ZXing\'s handling of 1D barcodes with poor alignment or low contrast is not ideal. To address this, I\'m developing a client-side preprocessor, including image resizing/cropping, brightness/contrast adjustments, and binarization techniques. The intention is to employ specific 1D formats like EAN_13 and EAN_8.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 618343110
    }
