        }
        lines {
          text: "1. **Optimal Fridge Placement**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - Store milk and yogurts on the **middle or top shelves (35\302\260F to 39\302\260F / 2\302\260C to 4\302\260C)**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - \342\232\240\357\270\217 *Avoid the fridge door*, where temperature fluctuates continuously."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. **Cheese Storage Secrets**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Hard & aged cheeses**: Wrap in parchment or wax paper instead of tight plastic wrap so moisture doesn\'t create mold."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Fresh cheeses**: Keep in airtight containers with a paper towel beneath to absorb excess whey."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. **Freezing Guide**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Milk**: Freeze leaving 1\342\200\2232 inches of headspace for expansion. Thaw in the fridge and shake well."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Grated Cheese**: Grate blocks and freeze with a dash of cornstarch in ziploc bags for easy sprinkling."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - **Yogurt**: Portion into ice cube trays for instant smoothie boosts."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "4. **Zero-Waste Transformations**:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   - If milk is nearing its date, heat it and add a splash of vinegar or lemon juice to craft fresh homemade ricotta in 10 minutes!`;"
